.TH WREX-ICMPV6 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-icmpv6 \- icmpv6 layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIicmpv6\fR \fB--icmpv6\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIicmpv6\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
ICMPv6 (RFC 4443) + NDP (RFC 4861) over IPv6. type 128/129 (echo request/reply) expose echo.id and echo.seq. NDP craft: RS (133, header only), RA (134: ndp.cur_hop_limit, ndp.ra_flags [m,o], ndp.router_lifetime, ndp.reachable_time, ndp.retrans_timer), NS (135: ndp.target), NA (136: ndp.na_flags [r,s,o] + ndp.target). Other types render the 4\-byte rest as icmpv6.rest raw bytes. checksum always covers the RFC 8200 §8.1 v6 pseudo\-header (proto 58) plus the whole message. NDP options dissect into the opt record section (opt.0.addr, …) and CRAFT through the options list grammar (tranche 17b: slla:MAC, tlla:MAC, mtu:N, prefix:…, raw:TYPE:HEX). MLDv1 (tranche 17b): types 130/131/132 carry the mld.addr multicast body (the v1 query's max\-response rides the code field). icmpv6 is terminal (the payload follows).
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 30; stacks on ipv6, hopopts, routing, frag, dstopts, ah (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --icmpv6-type).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-type=\fIINT\fR\fR
type (autofill: 128 echo request) Type u8. Default: 128.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-code=\fIINT\fR\fR
code (autofill: 0) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-checksum=\fIINT\fR\fR
checksum over v6 pseudo\-header+message (autofill: computed) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-echo\-id=\fIINT\fR\fR
echo identifier (types 128/129) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-echo\-seq=\fIINT\fR\fR
echo sequence (types 128/129) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-rest\fR
raw 4\-byte rest of header (non\-echo non\-NDP types) Type bytes. Default: .
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-cur_hop_limit=\fIINT\fR\fR
router advertisement: current hop limit Type u8. Default: 64.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\fR
router advertisement flags [m,o]; subpaths ndp.ra_flags.m / ndp.ra_flags.o Type flagset. Default: 0.
Bit names (MSB first): m, o. Aggregate \fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\fR sets the whole unit; per-bit \-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\-m sets one bit.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-router_lifetime=\fIINT\fR\fR
router advertisement: router lifetime (seconds) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-reachable_time=\fIINT\fR\fR
router advertisement: reachable time (ms) Type u32. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-retrans_timer=\fIINT\fR\fR
router advertisement: retransmit timer (ms) Type u32. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\fR
neighbor advertisement flags [r,s,o]; subpaths ndp.na_flags.r / .s / .o Type flagset. Default: 0.
Bit names (MSB first): r, s, o. Aggregate \fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\fR sets the whole unit; per-bit \-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\-r sets one bit.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-target=\fIINT\fR\fR
neighbor solicitation/advertisement: target address Type ipv6. Default: ::.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld\-addr=\fIINT\fR\fR
MLD multicast address (types 130/131/132; ff02::1 all\-nodes, ff02::2 all\-routers) Type ipv6. Default: ::.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld\-flags\fR
MLDv2 query flags [s] (suppress router\-side processing) Type flagset. Default: 0.
Bit names (MSB first): s. Aggregate \fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld\-flags\fR sets the whole unit; per-bit \-\-icmpv6\-mld\-flags\-s sets one bit.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld\-qrv=\fIINT\fR\fR
MLDv2 querier's robustness variable (3 bits) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld\-qqic=\fIINT\fR\fR
MLDv2 querier's query interval code Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld\-nsrcs=\fIINT\fR\fR
MLDv2 query source count (autofilled over mld.sources) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld\-sources\fR
MLDv2 query sources region (16\-byte addresses; hex on the CLI) Type bytes. Default: .
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-mld=\fIINT\fR\fR
MLDv2 report (type 143) record grammar: include:ADDR, exclude:ADDR, to_include:ADDR, to_exclude:ADDR, allow:ADDR, block:ADDR, bare IPv6 tokens continue the previous record as sources Type str. Default: .
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-options=\fIINT\fR\fR
NDP option TLV grammar, appended after the NDP body in order: slla:MAC, tlla:MAC, mtu:N, prefix:LEN,IP[,valid,preferred][,l][,a] (comma\-continued), raw:TYPE:HEX Type str. Default: .

.SH "RECORD SECTIONS"
Repeated record sections; dissected fields carry indexed paths (opt.0.field).

.TP
\fBopt\fR (dissect\-only)
NDP option TLVs after the NDP body (dissect\-only; indexed paths opt.0.addr, …)
  type (u8; default 0). option type (1 slla, 2 tlla)
  addr (mac; default 00:00:00:00:00:00). link\-layer address (slla/tlla options)
  data (bytes; default ). raw option data (other options)
.TP
\fBmcast\fR (dissect\-only)
MLDv2 multicast\-address records (dissect\-only; indexed paths mcast.0.*, …)
  type (u8; default 0). record type (1 include, 2 exclude, 3 change\-to\-include, 4 change\-to\-exclude, 5 allow, 6 block)
  nsrcs (u16; default 0). source count
  addr (ipv6; default ::). multicast address
  sources (bytes; default ). raw source addresses (16 bytes each)

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex fields icmpv6

